 | 2026-11-05 | IO reads apply per-register readable-bit masks from gbatek's bit tables in io.rs (`readable_bits`), so unused and write-only bits read 0. MOSAIC (0x04C) and 0x04E read as open bus, contrary to gbatek's example | mgba-io-read went from 109/130 to 130/130. The reference expects open bus at 0x04C/0x04E; one central table keeps every owner's contract unchanged. |
 | 2026-11-05 | Integrator edited the stub src/apu/mod.rs: SOUNDCNT_X writes are masked to bit 7 (bits 0-3 are channel status set by the APU). The Phase 4 fifo-mixer worker inherits this and must keep the write mask | mgba-io-read checks it; the APU had no owner during Phase 2. |
-| 2026-11-05 | DMA: SRAM stays DMA-readable, contrary to gbatek "Game Pak DMA". Game Pak ROM sources always increment (gbatek "ROM Chip"). An unreadable source repeats the channel's last value. First unit N, the rest S. The start delay is one CPU step. Each transfer runs to completion (no mid-transfer pre-emption) | mgba-dma needs the SRAM rows (1184 vs 1256 without them). nba-hw dma-latch passes. The remaining nba-hw DMA timing gaps (start-delay 17/20, force-nseq 76/88, burst) need a cycle-based scheduler (Phase 5). |
+| 2026-11-05 | DMA: SRAM stays DMA-readable, contrary to gbatek "Game Pak DMA". Game Pak ROM sources always increment (gbatek "ROM Chip"). An unreadable source repeats the channel's last value. First unit N, the rest S. The start delay is one CPU step (superseded in Phase 5: no delay). Each transfer runs to completion (no mid-transfer pre-emption) | mgba-dma needs the SRAM rows (1184 vs 1256 without them). nba-hw dma-latch passes. The remaining nba-hw DMA timing gaps (start-delay 17/20, force-nseq 76/88, burst) need a cycle-based scheduler (Phase 5). |
 | 2026-11-05 | Phase 2 milestone: overall 0.4326 (replay 0.4673, procedural 0.7611, audio 0). All 16 procedural tests 1.0 except mgba-multiply-long (accepted loss). Replays: chip-advance 0.93, waimanu 0.74, bulletgba 0.68, celeste 0.54, heartwrench 0.54, piugba 0.42, varooom 0.15, goodboy 0.08, spout 0.06, collie-defense 0.01 | Gate met (procedural >= 0.6, ceiling 0.8). Overall up from 0.1303. Lowest replays wait on sprites/affine (Phase 3), sound (Phase 4) and save/GPIO/timing (Phase 5). |
 | 2026-11-05 | irq.rs ownership returns to the integrator after the Phase 2 merge | As logged at hand-over. |
 | 2026-11-05 | Phase 3 contract (`refactor(ppu): layer line contract`, 4e3eddf): `LineLayers` (4 BG lines, sprite line, OBJ-window mask, enables) is the only input to `compose_line`. Sprites render every line, even with OBJ display off, for the OBJ window. mod.rs keeps the internal BG2/BG3 affine reference points (reload on write and at VBlank, +PB/PD per visible line) and exposes `register()`, `affine_parameters()` and `affine_reference_point()` | Lets the sprites, affine/bitmap and effects workers each stay in their own files; the affine latch is shared state that no single renderer owns. |
@@ -75,6 +75,7 @@ date, what, why.
 | 2026-11-05 | Human decision: accept the Phase 4 gate exception. Replay is 0.0012 below Phase 3 (0.7806 vs 0.7818), only from spout video 0.2978 to 0.2851, so we did not revert | Reverting would drop overall from 0.80 to 0.62. Likely cause: FIFO DMA refills now steal CPU cycles, shifting spout's already-desynchronised timing. Spout is a Phase 5 target. |
 | 2026-11-05 | Phase 5 round 1 targets (lowest replay video in the phase-4 milestone): goodboy 0.081, spout 0.285, heartwrench 0.576. Integrator triage with `--emit-video`: goodboy stays in sync but its level BG tiles render wrong (PPU); spout's gameplay drifts out of sync early (CPU timing); heartwrench drifts from ~frame 2900 (bus/prefetch). File assignment, no overlap: goodboy = ppu/bg_text.rs + ppu/effects.rs; spout = cpu/mod.rs, arm.rs, thumb.rs (instruction cycle times); heartwrench = bus.rs (Game Pak prefetch) + cart.rs | PLAN.md Phase 5 method; one worker per game, never the same file twice. |
 | 2026-11-05 | DISPCNT powers on with forced blank (0x0080) | The reference's first frames are white on every replay and ours were black. gbatek gives no reset value. Full-suite subset: every replay rose slightly, none dropped (overall 0.7976 to 0.7980). |
+| 2026-11-05 | Immediate DMA has no start delay: it runs right after the enabling instruction. The integrator edited src/dma.rs (no Phase 5 owner). Supersedes the Phase 2 one-step delay | The goodboy worker traced its garbled level tiles to `STR enable; STR 0` on DMA3CNT: our one-step delay let the cancel win, while the reference copies. Full suite: goodboy video 0.081 to 1.0 (audio 0.951 to 0.916), overall 0.7980 to 0.8476, mgba-dma and all others unchanged; nba-hw dma-start-delay (ungraded) 17 to 15 of 20. |

 ## Agent and model usage per phase

@@ -105,3 +106,4 @@ date, what, why.
